      "general": {
        "abstract": "The Intensive Monitoring of Forest Ecosystems (ICP-Forests Level II network) consists currently in 14 monitoring plots representing important Spanish Forest Ecosystems distributed throughout the Spanish mainland showing the most common forest situations of each country and representing rare or endemic situations.\r\n\r\nThe plot 10 Ppa represents a Pinus pinea pine forest located in the East of the Iberian peninsula.\r\nIt is a 41-60 years old monospecific regular high forest.\r\nIt has a quite uniform scrub layer, with little herbaceous layer.\r\nClimatic gradient is Thermomediterranean.\r\nTopography is flat. Soil is sandy (sub-coastal), type is Gleyc Arenosol but with moderate drainage as there is a very shallow water table.\r\n",
